Implement a strict Content Security Policy by removing unsafe-inline and unsafe-eval and allowing only trusted domains.

Upgrade all outdated libraries like jQuery to the latest secure version and avoid unsafe DOM manipulation methods.

Disable deprecated TLS versions and weak cipher suites such as 3DES and enforce TLS 1.2 or higher.

Sanitize all application outputs to prevent exposure of internal file paths and sensitive system information.

Set HttpOnly and SameSite attributes on cookies to protect against XSS and CSRF attacks.
